Description: Implements group-based trajectory modeling (GBTM) for longitudinal
    criminology data analysis. The package provides functions to identify distinct
    developmental trajectories in offending behavior over time using finite mixture
    models. Supports various outcome distributions (Poisson, zero-inflated Poisson,
    Gaussian), polynomial trajectory shapes, covariate effects on group membership
    and trajectory shapes, and comprehensive model selection tools including BIC and
    cross-validation. Based on the methodological framework developed by Nagin (2005)
    and extends it with modern statistical learning approaches for improved model
    selection and validation.
